# Summary
This report was valid when filed against commit `7094731` (`Type all stored system metadata values`).

That change introduced typed `ContentEncoding` storage with a maximum-length check in `s3-types`, and `SystemMetadata::strip_aws_chunked_content_encoding` rebuilt the header with `", "` and used `ContentEncoding::new(...).expect(...)`. A client could supply a valid near-limit `Content-Encoding`, have it expand during rebuild, fail revalidation, and hit the `expect` panic.

Two later changes altered the state:

- Commit `bf85822` (`Move metadata size validation to HTTP boundary`) removed per-value maximum-length validation from the stored metadata types in [`crates/s3-types/src/lib.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/s3-types/src/lib.rs:98), which made the specific length-growth reproduction from this report no longer valid on `main`.
- Commit `2802c9f` (`Harden aws-chunked content-encoding stripping`) removed the panic boundary entirely in [`crates/server-core/src/system_metadata.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-core/src/system_metadata.rs:344) and propagated errors normally from the HTTP layer in [`crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:3478).

Current status: the original finding was valid at introduction time, later became stale because the triggering max-length invariant was removed, and is now fully hardened because `strip_aws_chunked_content_encoding` no longer panics.

# Validation
## Historical validation
- Commit `7094731` introduced typed `ContentEncoding` values with per-value max-length validation and the `expect`-based rebuild path.
- At that point, the reported reproduction was valid: the rebuilt value could grow because the helper normalized with `", "`, `ContentEncoding::new(...)` could fail on length, and the `expect` would panic.

## Current validation
- Commit `bf85822` removed the stored-value max-length validation, leaving only header-byte validation in [`crates/s3-types/src/lib.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/s3-types/src/lib.rs:103). That means the exact `InvalidLength` panic described in the original report is no longer reproducible on current `main`.
- Commit `2802c9f` changed `strip_aws_chunked_content_encoding` to return `Result<(), ServerError>` and removed `expect` entirely in [`crates/server-core/src/system_metadata.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-core/src/system_metadata.rs:344).
- The HTTP request path now propagates that result normally in [`crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs`](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:3478).
- Regression coverage was added in `server-core` for:
  - normal `aws-chunked` stripping
  - preserving existing spacing shape as much as possible
  - comma-only forms such as `gzip,aws-chunked,br`
  - leading `aws-chunked` with a long remaining token

# Evidence
