# Resolution
Resolved by commit `2802c9f` (`Harden aws-chunked content-encoding stripping`).

Notes:
- The report remains historically valid against commit `7094731`.
- The exact `InvalidLength` reproduction became stale after `bf85822` moved aggregate size enforcement to the HTTP boundary and removed per-value maximum-length validation from stored metadata types.
- The code has now been hardened anyway so this path does not panic even if future validation rules change again.
